diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 2aa7d97..4fd7c3d 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -5,9 +5,19 @@ The game stays on the headphones you already use. Secure Boot stays on.
 Open the app. Three steps.
 
 1. Confirm the headphones.
-2. Hear a step, then a shot.
+2. Pick a tune (Footsteps or Everyday) and press Play. You hear a few steps and a boom without the tune, then with it.
 3. Turn on. Press Yes if Windows asks.
 
-Footstep hit raises only the short step. Surround quiet turns the room down. Leave the game on those headphones.
+Footstep boost lifts the step range. Footsteps is the competitive tune. Everyday is gentler for music and chat.
+Surround 7.1 is advanced and needs your headphones set to 7.1 in Windows.
 
-Equalizer APO must already be installed. That is the piece that runs the mix on the headphones. Your own device waits until it is signed.
+Safe to use next to other audio setups
+- Our settings live in their own folder inside the Equalizer APO config folder (JesusKpekpes\chain.txt).
+- The only change to your config.txt is one include line. A one-time backup is saved as config.txt.jesuskpekpes-backup.
+- Turn off only rewrites our own file. Your Equalizer APO, HeSuVi, Rara or other setup is never edited.
+- Remove completely (tray menu) deletes our folder and that one line.
+- If we find another setup (HeSuVi, VST plugins, other EQ) we tell you and leave it alone.
+
+The tunes are starting points to adjust by ear. The loudness is lowered automatically so loud sounds do not distort, so you may want to raise the headphone volume a little.
+
+Equalizer APO must already be installed. That is the piece that runs the mix on the headphones. An automatic installer comes next. Your own device waits until it is signed.
